# Session entry point: ephemeral by design, rewritten each session.
START_HERE.md

# In-process and working files, including the message a commit is given with
# -F. Gitignored so that naming it on the command line can never put it into
# the commit it describes.
.ephemera/

# Python build and cache artifacts. The pack is installed editable, so the
# egg-info lands beside the source rather than in a build directory.
#
# `build/` is here because building a wheel to check what it carries leaves one,
# and the gate then GRADES it: measured 2026-08-28, `analyse` and `types` both
# failed against copied sources under `python/build/`. The walk honours gitignore,
# so ignoring it is what keeps the gate measuring the pack rather than a copy.
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
build/

# bolt writes its evidence to .bolt-<iso8601> at the base unless told otherwise,
# so a run from the repository root leaves one of these behind. Run it with
# --output-dir .ephemera/gate to keep evidence where working files belong.
.bolt-*/

# Rust build output. Cargo.lock is committed for a binary and omitted for a
# library, and this is a library, so a consumer resolves its own versions.
rust/target/
rust/Cargo.lock

# coverage writes this beside the pack when the shared jig runs its tests
.coverage
python/.coverage

# The adopted jig links. `toolbox/jigs.yaml` declares the set and `link-jigs`
# makes them. They are ignored because a tracked symlink stores its target path
# as content, so committing one encodes where ../toolbox happens to sit and
# hands a clone six paths that resolve to nothing.
#
# Named one at a time rather than as `bolt.*.yaml`, because that glob would also
# swallow `bolt.wrench-quality.yaml` and `bolt.wrench.definitions.yaml`, which
# are this repository's own files and ARE tracked.
#
# `bin/` cannot be ignored wholesale for the same reason: it holds wrench's own
# checkers beside two links, so the two are named.
bolt.common-quality.yaml
bolt.go-std-quality.yaml
bolt.python-std-quality.yaml
bolt.secrets.yaml
adapters/
config/
bin/suppression-register.py
bin/test-traceability.py
